  "slug": "slow-cooker-chicken-cordon-bleu",
  "name": "Slow Cooker Chicken Cordon Bleu",
  "recipe_type": "main",
  "brief_description": "Layers of chicken, ham and Swiss cheese simmer in a creamy sauce while topped with stuffing mix.",
  "cuisine": "French Inspired",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Mix together the cream of chicken soup and milk in a small bowl. Pour enough of the soup into a slow cooker to cover the bottom. Layer chicken breasts over the sauce. Cover with slices of ham and then Swiss cheese. Pour the remaining soup over the layers, stirring a little to distribute between layers. Sprinkle the stuffing on top, and drizzle butter over stuffing. Cover, and cook on Low for 4 to 6 hours, or 2 to 3 hours on High."
    }
  ],
